<script>
  var key = "doesntmatterreallydoesnt"

  if(sessionStorage.getItem(key) === null) {
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, "test1")

    location.hash = "forward"
    setTimeout(() => {
      history.back()
      setTimeout(() => {
        alert("1:" + location.hash)
        location.href = location.href
      }, 250)
    }, 250)
  } else if(sessionStorage.getItem(key) === "test1") {
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, "test2")

    // This is the same location.hash = "forward", but now it refreshes the page
    history.forward()
  } else if(sessionStorage.getItem(key) === "test2") {
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, "test3")

    alert("2: " + location.hash)
    history.back()
  } else if(sessionStorage.getItem(key) === "test3") {
    sessionStorage.removeItem(key)

    alert("3: done")
  }
</script>
```
Is an attempt at testing that forward history doesn't get deleted. However, in Chrome fragment navigation through `location.hash` doesn't seem to create a history entry (despite the equivalent through `<a>.click()` doing so) so it's not super useful. However, testing manually through the UI it does seem that Chrome does not delete forward history so I think that is indeed what we should go with.
